cutoff expansion: -alpha^2 + alpha + 2/eps^2 - 1/6
finite part C(alpha) = -alpha^2 + alpha - 1/6 ; equals -(alpha^2 - alpha + 1/6): True
alpha = 1/4: zeta(-1, a) + zeta(-1, 1 - a) = 0.0208333333, -B_2(alpha) = 0.0208333333
alpha = 1/3: zeta(-1, a) + zeta(-1, 1 - a) = 0.0555555556, -B_2(alpha) = 0.0555555556
alpha = 1/2: zeta(-1, a) + zeta(-1, 1 - a) = 0.0833333333, -B_2(alpha) = 0.0833333333
alpha -> 0: C -> -1/6 = 2 zeta(-1), the untwisted value
